  "jobTitle": "Principal Software Engineer",
  "summary": "I build and lead the engineering behind complex business software, from the database ledger up to the AI layer.\n\nFor eight years I've been the technical lead of Flyntlok, a multi-tenant ERP that equipment dealers across North America and Australia run their whole business on: sales, service, rentals, inventory and accounting. I architected its rental system and its domain-driven GraphQL backend, designed its accounting, tax and multi-currency foundations, and today own the overhaul of its inventory and costing system.\n\nI also lead the company's AI work. I built a Kubernetes-based agent platform where AI agents investigate data-integrity cases overnight in a sandbox, backed by an evaluation harness and a review console, and I'm leading a customer-facing MCP service for AI-driven reporting.\n\nOn the people side, I've run engineering hiring since 2019, built a new engineering office in Boston, mentored most of the team, and sit on the management team as the technical voice in executive decisions.\n\nWhat I'm good at:\n• Turning messy, high-stakes systems (money, inventory, tax) into correct, auditable ones\n• Designing backends and data models that a growing team can build on for years\n• Putting AI agents into production responsibly: sandboxing, evaluation, human review\n• Growing engineers and building the team and practices around the code\n\nStack: TypeScript/Node.js, GraphQL, SQL/MySQL, gRPC, Kubernetes (GKE), GitOps, Google Cloud, BigQuery, React/Next.js, LLM agents (Claude), MCP.\n\nInterested in principal/staff engineering and engineering-leadership roles, especially in AI platforms, vertical SaaS and fintech/ERP.",
